  "live_records": {
    "q-162972": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162972",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "The lamina $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,-y\\le x\\le y\\}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=6{x}^{2}.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=6{x}^{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot 6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}6{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-y}^{y}6{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2y[{\\int }_{-y}^{y}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2y\\cdot {[{x}^{3}]}_{x=-y}^{x=y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2y\\cdot 2{y}^{3}\\text{ }\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{4}{5}{y}^{5}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
