    "q-162977": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162977",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "The lamina $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,1\\le x\\le {e}^{y}\\}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{xy}.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{xy}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot \\frac{1}{xy}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{y}}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{x=1}^{x={e}^{y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(9-1) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
