    "q-163066": {
      "dom_id": "step-q163066",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The lamina $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3y,\\,0\\le y\\le 1\\}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=5xy.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=5xy.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot 5xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}5{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3y}5{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}5y{\\int }_{0}^{3y}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}5y{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=3y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}5y(9{y}^{3}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}45{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[9{y}^{5}]_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
